{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>I too will do this to you.</b> I will do what you plotted to do — so that the covenant be broken and nullified also on My side, as I said: when you are Mine as a people, I will be ״to you for an Elohim״ (Leviticus 26:12), without intermediary." "<b>And I will appoint over you terror.</b> I will appoint over you officers of terror, in the manner of ״And to the others He said in my hearing: Pass through the city after him and strike; let your eye not spare and do not pity״ (Ezekiel 9:5)." "<b>And your enemies shall eat it.</b> As was the case in the days of the Judges, as it says: ״And it was, when Israel had sown, that Midian and Amalek and the children of the east came up״ (Judges 6:3)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The word בִּלְתִּי אֶמְצָעִי ('without intermediary') modifies HaShem's direct relationship with Israel; the point is that the covenant's annulment removes that immediacy."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:16.373738954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}